<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 17:45:13 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Iran engages US in 'intensive' negotiations to avert fresh war outbreak</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261102-iran-engages-us-in-intensive-negotiations-to-avert-fresh-war-outbreak</link><description>
Tehran on Monday said that the country was holding "intensive" indirect talks with Washington to avoid a fresh round of US attacks on Iran ahead of the US midterm elections this week. Foreign ministry spokesperson Esmaeil Baghaei shared Iranian plans to reopen blockaded energy corridor, the Strait of Hormuz, if the US were to meet its demands.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/18a41438-d6dc-11f1-b1cd-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-17T081002Z-2072440926-RC2W4OA50VW1-RTRMADP-3-IRAQ-CONFERENCE-OIC.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/18a41438-d6dc-11f1-b1cd-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-17T081002Z-2072440926-RC2W4OA50VW1-RTRMADP-3-IRAQ-CONFERENCE-OIC.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7fe13154-d6db-11f1-9659-5b23d832e19d</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 17:42:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/18a41438-d6dc-11f1-b1cd-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-17T081002Z-2072440926-RC2W4OA50VW1-RTRMADP-3-IRAQ-CONFERENCE-OIC.jpg">© Ahmed Saad, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Iran offers deal on Hormuz Strait, Netanyahu wants to 'finish the job'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-iran-offers-deal-on-hormuz-strait-netanyahu-wants-to-finish-the-job</link><description>
Iran said Monday it had a two-day plan to reopen the Strait of Hormuz and resume nuclear talks with the United States, shortening a process originally expected to take seven days. Israel's Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said he wanted to "finish the job" first. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Angela Diffley has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c0624b8-d6da-11f1-87b4-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-b0a449cf.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c0624b8-d6da-11f1-87b4-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-b0a449cf.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f50a4f94-d6d9-11f1-a9db-9b6af090a5e5</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 17:04:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Petition to ban French right-wing TV channel clears 500,000 signatures after racist killing</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261102-petition-to-ban-french-right-wing-tv-channel-clears-500-000-signatures-after-racist-killing</link><description>
A petition calling for right-wing television channel CNews to be taken off-air cleared half a million signatures on Monday after a Frenchman shot and killed a French national of Congolese origin and wounded seven others. The 39-year-old shooter is believed to have been an avid watcher of CNews, which is owned by ultra-conservative billionaire Vincent Bolloré and has been accused of promoting far-right anti-immigrant views. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f2098d52-d6b9-11f1-99d5-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B3JA8MX.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f2098d52-d6b9-11f1-99d5-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B3JA8MX.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d26a47d4-d6d7-11f1-bf04-a925b2fb2562</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 16:53:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f2098d52-d6b9-11f1-99d5-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B3JA8MX.jpg">© Stéphane de Sakutin, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>British adventurer arrives back at mother's home after 28-year journey</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-british-adventurer-arrives-back-at-mother-s-home-after-28-year-journey</link><description>
British adventurer Karl Bushby enjoyed an emotional reunion with his mother and family on Monday, as he arrived back home after a 28-year, 50,000-kilometre trek from South America, crossing four continents on foot.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f06a2dc2-d6db-11f1-bc19-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/mini3-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f06a2dc2-d6db-11f1-bc19-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/mini3-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">130d557a-d6dc-11f1-bcef-5b6dff722978</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 16:45:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>What changes if Democrats win a majority in Congress?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261102-what-changes-if-democrats-win-a-majority-in-congress</link><description>
Americans head to the polls on Tuesday for the US midterm elections, which could flip the majority in one or both houses of Congress from the Republicans to the Democrats. What would a Democratic majority mean for the country's political landscape, and how might Democrats move to keep President Donald Trump in check?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d61f8930-c86c-11f1-ab9a-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/main-pouvoir-congres-democrate.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d61f8930-c86c-11f1-ab9a-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/main-pouvoir-congres-democrate.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ce5e5364-d6d3-11f1-805b-730585255cda</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 16:29:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d61f8930-c86c-11f1-ab9a-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/main-pouvoir-congres-democrate.jpg">© France Médias Monde Graphics Studio</source><dc:creator>Romain HOUEIX</dc:creator></item><item><category>arts24</category><title>A musical overview of trans-European punk</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261102-a-musical-overview-of-trans-european-punk</link><description>
This week on arts24, we're bringing you a double dose of European punk. Elias Bender Rønnenfelt is a singer with Copenhagen's finest post-punk export, Iceage. The group is currently touring Europe, and he is stopping off in Paris this week to play the Pitchfork festival solo. We also welcome Chris Hughes from Fat Dog. Born in South London in 2020 during lockdown, Fat Dog have just released their second album "Cancel Me (I'm Tired)", which will thrill synth lovers and punk rockers alike. They are currently touring France and Europe.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2a461c70-d6d4-11f1-a42a-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-66b709a8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2a461c70-d6d4-11f1-a42a-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-66b709a8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1d6266ca-d6d5-11f1-9a0b-6300e6e4e62b</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 16:05:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marjorie HACHE</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel's president begins process of coalition government negotiations</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-israel-s-president-begins-process-of-coalition-government-negotiations</link><description>
Israel's President Isaac Herzog begins the process of coalition government negotiations this week. One possibility is for the centrist opposition bloc to form a government with the Arab parties, which would oust current Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. Protests for and against such a coalition this weekend made it clear the Israeli public is divided over the idea.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7037ab46-d6d3-11f1-8ca1-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d7c5bf92.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7037ab46-d6d3-11f1-8ca1-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d7c5bf92.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2b76929c-d6d3-11f1-bf20-dbdcb2dc92af</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 15:57:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Down to Earth</category><title>Scientists begin tests on human composting, an eco-friendly alternative to burials and cremation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/down-to-earth/20261102-scientists-begin-tests-on-human-composting-an-eco-friendly-alternative-to-burials-and-cremation</link><description>
Humans have caused irreversible changes to our planet in their time on Earth, pollution that continues even in death. Cremation relies heavily on fossil fuels, while traditional burials take up land. So is there a more eco-friendly way to honour our loved ones? French scientists are exploring the possibility of composting human bodies, a process that returns those who have died to the earth. Our Down to Earth team reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/843c4600-d6cf-11f1-97d1-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/8bf0ba12-5b39-4423-8a17-a01efb09b988.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/843c4600-d6cf-11f1-97d1-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/8bf0ba12-5b39-4423-8a17-a01efb09b988.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9a7f249a-d6d0-11f1-acab-4d80a1b698eb</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 15:41:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Valérie DEKIMPE</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nine dead in small plane crash near Trump's Florida home</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-nine-dead-in-small-plane-crash-near-trump-s-florida-home</link><description>
Nine people were killed Sunday when the Learjet they were travelling in plummeted into a neighbourhood in southern Florida, just miles from US President Donald Trump's resort home of Mar-a-Lago, officials said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1373b412-d6cf-11f1-99ce-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/mini2-5.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1373b412-d6cf-11f1-99ce-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/mini2-5.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b016d92a-d6cf-11f1-9bcd-cb669b5f6870</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 15:33:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Inflation, war and corruption: Will anger at Trump see Republicans punished at midterms?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-inflation-war-and-corruption-will-anger-at-trump-see-republicans-punished-at-midterms</link><description>
Donald Trump and his Republican Party will make last-gasp pitches to US midterm voters Monday to hold back a predicted Democrat wave that could take over Congress and impose tight political constraints on the president for the first time in two years. With Trump's popularity at an historic low, many are predicting voters will punish the Republican Party at the polls. France 24's Philip Turle takes a closer look.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c8075c88-d6d1-11f1-8626-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261102-160514-160923-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c8075c88-d6d1-11f1-8626-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261102-160514-160923-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cdf9c6b2-d6d1-11f1-a4e9-1f59e0efed86</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 15:30:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Heading into the midterms, 'no US president in recent times has been as unpopular as Donald Trump'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/heading-into-the-midterms-no-us-president-in-recent-times-has-been-as-unpopular-as-donald-trump</link><description>
Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Richard Johnson, Senior Lecturer in US Politics at Queen Mary University of London. He says that "Donald Trump is damaged goods at this point in his presidency." With this uncompromising assessment, Johnson takes us through the political forces shaping the 2026 US midterm elections. Far from assuming that Trump's formidable campaigning instincts can once again mobilize Republican voters, Johnson questions whether the president's political influence has become a liability for the very party he once transformed. He points to a potentially significant realignment within the American electorate. Economic grievances, rising living costs, trade disputes and disillusionment with the war in Iran appear, in Johnson's reading, to be weakening important elements of the coalition that sustained Trump's return to power. Particularly consequential is the possibility that Latino voters, agricultural communities and sections of the MAGA electorate may be reconsidering their political loyalties or withdrawing from electoral participation altogether.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bdbaa30e-d6cf-11f1-ab72-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261102-150111-151452-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bdbaa30e-d6cf-11f1-ab72-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261102-150111-151452-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c3190430-d6cf-11f1-96bf-b1807fb543aa</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 15:25:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukraine and Russia report fake emergency alerts after cyberattacks target apps</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-and-russia-report-fake-emergency-alerts-after-cyberattacks-target-apps</link><description>
Authorities in Ukraine and Russia said their emergency alert mobile apps had been targeted by cyberattacks, with users in Ukraine receiving false warnings of an imminent nuclear threat. Moscow said that hackers had sent fake emergency alerts after gaining access to the Russian Emergency Situations Ministry’s mobile app, and that efforts were ongoing to restore the app's functionality.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/30e69a66-d6cd-11f1-800e-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-471ee61c.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/30e69a66-d6cd-11f1-800e-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-471ee61c.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9a629f90-d6cc-11f1-b20f-673158319541</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 15:06:41 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US Midterms: Will Gen Z enthusiasm help turn Michigan Senate blue?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-us-midterms-will-gen-z-enthusiasm-help-turn-michigan-senate-blue</link><description>
Michigan’s Senate seat is a must-win for the Democratic Party as it seeks to take control of the upper house of Congress. There’s a surge of energy behind progressive candidate Abdul El-Sayed, especially among younger voters. But can Gen Z's enthusiasm translate into votes and help Democrats win a critical Senate seat?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4434a4ec-d6cc-11f1-94f1-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-815f4d3f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4434a4ec-d6cc-11f1-94f1-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-815f4d3f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">33801bc8-d6cb-11f1-b8df-272a86085fe5</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 15:03:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Could Argentina’s Patagonia become a haven for data centres?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-could-argentina-s-patagonia-become-a-haven-for-data-centres</link><description>
Around the world, citizens and lawmakers are increasingly pushing back against the construction of data centres, citing noise pollution, massive power consumption and general unsightliness. But Argentina's President Javier Milei wants more of them - and the government thinks it may have found an ideal location, in the vast open steppes of Patagonia.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/490a7712-d6c7-11f1-b522-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261102-144234-144418-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/490a7712-d6c7-11f1-b522-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261102-144234-144418-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4e1a60b4-d6c7-11f1-af9f-414644bd4048</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 14:16:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French school protests resume on smaller scale after autumn break</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-french-school-protests-resume-on-smaller-scale-after-autumn-break</link><description>
French high school student protests resumed on Monday on a ​much smaller scale than in past weeks as pupils returned from a two-week break, with youngsters trying to blockade a few high schools in Paris, Marseille and Rennes.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bfb21bec-d6c5-11f1-b1dd-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261102-144020-144142-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bfb21bec-d6c5-11f1-b1dd-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261102-144020-144142-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c4b3ad86-d6c5-11f1-bc67-5b2ce6a8686d</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 14:15:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Sour grapes? Dems shocked as Haley Stevens breaks ranks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-sour-grapes-dems-shocked-as-haley-stevens-breaks-ranks</link><description>
France 24’s Fraser Jackson takes a look at the state of play one day ahead of crucial midterm elections in the US as both Democrats and Republicans make their final bids for votes. Meanwhile, Michigan Democrat Haley Stevens has rocked the state’s Senate race by endorsing Republican Mike Rogers over Democratic candidate Abdul El-Sayed. Stevens lost the Michigan Democrats' Senate primary to El-Sayed in a bitterly contested race, leading some to accuse her of sour grapes.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/85c34c60-d6c2-11f1-84d0-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261102-140324-140754-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/85c34c60-d6c2-11f1-84d0-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261102-140324-140754-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8aa0200a-d6c2-11f1-b9c1-bd5d82051c67</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 13:54:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Fresh wave of fridge cyberattacks hits European supermarkets</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-fresh-wave-of-fridge-cyberattacks-hits-european-supermarkets</link><description>
Stores and supermarkets across Belgium, Luxembourg, Finland, Estonia and Sweden all reported early Monday abrupt temperature spikes in their fridges and freezers in an apparent cyberattack targeting refrigeration units. The incidents follow a similar attack that hit hundreds of supermarkets across France in October, triggering food loss and fires.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/071116b6-d6b0-11f1-99f9-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D64Y2DM.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/071116b6-d6b0-11f1-99f9-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D64Y2DM.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5631e158-d6bf-11f1-aa7d-61c7f4643f18</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 13:40:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/071116b6-d6b0-11f1-99f9-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D64Y2DM.jpg">© Fredrik Sandberg, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Italian journalists under police protection as threats rise across the country</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-italian-journalists-under-police-protection-as-threats-rise-across-the-country</link><description>
Italy is the European country with the largest number of journalists under police protection. There, journalism is a profession particularly susceptible to threats and intimidation, but the European Union's measures to protect press freedom are slow to be implemented. FRANCE 24's team has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8bb11af2-d6b9-11f1-9e68-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-0bf09737.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8bb11af2-d6b9-11f1-9e68-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-0bf09737.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">112b5a04-d6b9-11f1-8741-83bfd1635af1</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 13:20:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>US midterm elections: North Carolina farmers hit hard by inflation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261102-us-midterm-elections-north-carolina-farmers-hit-hard-by-inflation</link><description>
On the eve of the midterm elections, US President Donald Trump's unpopularity is impacting Republicans across the board. Many states with seats once considered Republican strongholds are now on shaky ground. One of them is North Carolina, a rural state where one in five jobs is tied to agriculture.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6dfd6204-d6be-11f1-ade0-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-cbd2a019.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6dfd6204-d6be-11f1-ade0-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-cbd2a019.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5fb826f6-d480-11f1-bc79-6b6f931b1085</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 13:13:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Fanny ALLARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Michigan Democrat's endorsement of Republican ruffles critical Senate race</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-michigan-democrat-s-endorsement-of-republican-ruffles-critical-senate-race-1</link><description>
A prominent Michigan Democrat endorsed Republican Mike Rogers on Sunday, giving President Donald Trump's Republicans an unexpected boost in a critical US Senate race two days before midterm elections that will decide control of Congress.
